35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found that only two firms can dig here, and they worry about the clay. The depot notes say we can keep the park open in stages.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Victoria, the ledger is brutal. Planted ground costs triple to maintain, and the gap is widening. The habitat fund only covers planting, not the hard surfaces.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@May, that is a heavy burden. My findings are similar. The civic hall apron has been patched three times, while the upstream basin remains sound.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@May, that confirms my fear. The roll is down to seven, and the eastern avenue trees died from neglect. Who is left to do the basic care?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, two firms is a bottleneck. My data shows drainage callouts doubled and heat spikes are severe. The ground is failing, not just the people.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, that is worrying. If the ground fails, the two firms will be stuck. I hope the phasing helps us avoid that.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, your apron data is a warning. If hard surfaces decay, the city pays the triple upkeep penalty. We need to minimize that liability.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, exactly. The basin lasted because it was simple. The apron failed because it was complex. We must choose what endures, not what impresses.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, simplicity is key. The avenue trees died because aftercare was omitted. We need a plan that fits the seven staff we actually have, not the eighteen we lost.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, seven staff is a hard limit. My crossing data shows people stick to firm ground. We need a plan that respects the drainage reality, not just the aesthetic.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I am glad you are looking at the crossings. I worry the clay will make the digging slow. I hope the phasing keeps us safe.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, the clay is a headache, but the ledger is the real killer. If we plant too much, the city drowns in triple costs. Keep it simple.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, the clay is a challenge, but the apron’s decay is the true lesson. We must build for the long, quiet years, not the opening day.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, the phasing helps, but the staffing gap is the real risk. We cannot rely on casuals for daily care.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the clay is a nuisance, but the drainage failure is the crisis. If the ground floods, the phasing is irrelevant. We must design for the water, not just the dig.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I hear you. The water is scary. I just hope the two firms can finish before the rain comes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, the water is a headache, but the ledger is the real killer. If we plant too much, the city drowns in triple costs. Keep it simple.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Shunichi, you are right. The water is the true test. I will look for a plan that lets the ground breathe, not one that fights it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, the water is critical, but the staffing is the bottleneck. We need a plan that seven people can actually sustain, not one that requires a ghost army.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, seven staff is a hard limit. My crossing data shows people stick to firm ground. We need a plan that respects the drainage reality, not just the aesthetic.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
